{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia","id":1481774,"title":"Learning from Goetia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-23T13:48:03-07:00","id":1481774,"title":"Learning from Goetia","content":"So, I am running a Changeling game, and one of the players has found a synesi leading to an Astral realm reflecting the Burning and Evacuation of Finmark during WW2. Anyway, the question I am getting to is that this particular character is very into trying to learn ritual knowledge and stuff to use. Now, in relation the Spirits and Ghosts it is easy since they have established ritual magics to teach. Like Ceremonies and Rites, but here I am more at a loss. But it seems to me that most Ephemeral creatures can teach people limited magics. Akharatoi, Fiends from Duat specifically, Spirits, Ghosts, Angels, Elpidos, and so on all seem to be able to do that in some form. So, logically I would think that non-mages should be able to learn from Goetia as well. But, I am not sure if there is an established system for this or if I should homebrew something. A lil help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T14:31:42-07:00","id":1481776,"title":"","content":"The first challenge to overcome is that I believe the Lost cannot access a Synesi normally. The mage core book compares using a Key in the Synesi to astrally projecting through it, but changelings can only reach the Oneiros' dream layer at best. This is because during the Durance, their Pattern was fundamentally warped by the Keeper. The effect of this supernatural madness severs their ability to enter the Temenos, the collective soul of humanity and the Realms beyond (same as vampires, werewolves, etc) by traditional means. So one option is to have a Mind mage journey alongside them. There is always the alternative of finding a backdoor, something like an area in the Hsil/Shadow or Underworld that has a path to the Astral. But where in the Astral is anyone's guess, could be the Sideral Wastes, the Dreaming Earth, a random realm in the Temenos or many more. <br /> <br /> But once you reach the Astral, there aren't many rituals, but there is still a lot that can be learned. They can try to find lost lore on changelings and the True Fae, with the caveat that the Astral warps objectivity based on popular opinion, so cross checking any leads is an important sanity check. They could look for a mage realm for a Legacy or Mystery Cult that study the True Fae, although that has its own risks as well. Researching Oneiromancy could lead them to better understand its nature or perhaps develop unique variations of its abilities. Lastly, you could use the Familiar rite mechanics in <i>Hunter, The Vigil: Witchfinders</i> as a basis for an astral familiar. Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T14:32:32-07:00","id":1481777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia#post1481774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I am running a Changeling game, and one of the players has found a synesi leading to an Astral realm reflecting the Burning and Evacuation of Finmark during WW2. Anyway, the question I am getting to is that this particular character is very into trying to learn ritual knowledge and stuff to use. Now, in relation the Spirits and Ghosts it is easy since they have established ritual magics to teach. Like Ceremonies and Rites, but here I am more at a loss. But it seems to me that most Ephemeral creatures can teach people limited magics. Akharatoi, Fiends from Duat specifically, Spirits, Ghosts, Angels, Elpidos, and so on all seem to be able to do that in some form. So, logically I would think that non-mages should be able to learn from Goetia as well. But, I am not sure if there is an established system for this or if I should homebrew something. A lil help?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the 1e blue book Second Sight had something on it, basically buying each effect/spell as a separate merit, changing costs to WP.<br /> But don't take my word for it, either check it out for yourself or homebrew stuff, that is perfectly valid for one's game too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T14:33:05-07:00","id":1481778,"title":"","content":"Goetia feel like they\u2019d impart mundane knowledge, just deeper and broader than usually expected. Like getting the digests of every academic paper a Wikipedia page links to.<br /> <br /> For magic stuff, maybe they can teach relevant Ritual Sorcery (the stuff expanded in Mummy)? Even then, I suspect the changelings will have to intuit and deduce the rituals from the Goetias\u2019 actions and words, rather than have the Goetia hand it to them all wrapped up, unless they contacted a Goetia who should logically know sorcerous rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T14:47:47-07:00","id":1481784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia?p=1481776#post1481776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first challenge to overcome is that I believe the Lost cannot access a Synesi normally. The mage core book compares using a Key in the Synesi to astrally projecting through it, but changelings can only reach the Oneiros' dream layer at best. This is because during the Durance, their Pattern was fundamentally warped by the Keeper. The effect of this supernatural madness severs their ability to enter the Temenos, the collective soul of humanity and the Realms beyond (same as vampires, werewolves, etc) by traditional means. So one option is to have a Mind mage journey alongside them. There is always the alternative of finding a backdoor, something like an area in the Hsil/Shadow or Underworld that has a path to the Astral. But where in the Astral is anyone's guess, could be the Sideral Wastes, the Dreaming Earth, a random realm in the Temenos or many more.<br /> <br /> But once you reach the Astral, there aren't many rituals, but there is still a lot that can be learned. They can try to find lost lore on changelings and the True Fae, with the caveat that the Astral warps objectivity based on popular opinion, so cross checking any leads is an important sanity check. They could look for a mage realm for a Legacy or Mystery Cult that study the True Fae, although that has its own risks as well. Researching Oneiromancy could lead them to better understand its nature or perhaps develop unique variations of its abilities. Lastly, you could use the Familiar rite mechanics in <i>Hunter, The Vigil: Witchfinders</i> as a basis for an astral familiar. Hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Normally, you would be correct in the sense that most people can't go beyond the surface level of their own Oneiros. But Synesi are different in that according to the second edition corebook allows anyone with the key(or another means of entering) to access it while sleeping or meditating. In the case of this Synesi the key is burning herbs, food, alcohol, and something valuable at the location as it used to be an ancient sacrificial spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T15:15:11-07:00","id":1481788,"title":"","content":"Looking into the matter I have found that there is a ritual magic type connected to the Astral, specifically Obcasus rites connected to the Primordial Dream and the Dark Mother who resides in the Anima Mundi. So, that establishes a precedent..if one for a specific supernatural template. So, it is worth pondering if there is more to it than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:22:29-07:00","id":1481795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia#post1481774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it seems to me that most Ephemeral creatures can teach people limited magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you got this assumption, considering that most of the examples are either &quot;agent of fate bestows power on a mortal as part of its divine mission&quot; or &quot;this applies a template to a character.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, logically I would think that non-mages should be able to learn from Goetia as well. But, I am not sure if there is an established system for this or if I should homebrew something. A lil help? </div> </div> </div>The closest we get to this from Goetia is that Dreamtime Goetia can lend their Influence over the world to people who go through the appropriate channels. Goetia mostly stick to the Astral, because the routes out of it are so few and far-between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T10:55:52-07:00","id":1481851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia?p=1481795#post1481795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where you got this assumption, considering that most of the examples are either &quot;agent of fate bestows power on a mortal as part of its divine mission&quot; or &quot;this applies a template to a character.&quot;<br /> <br /> The closest we get to this from Goetia is that Dreamtime Goetia can lend their Influence over the world to people who go through the appropriate channels. Goetia mostly stick to the Astral, because the routes out of it are so few and far-between.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw an outline of that from the Dreaming Earth section of the <i>Astral Realms</i> book. Would there be anywhere else that the details are fleshed out or some sample Dreamborne are presented? Would the Influences be fueled by Essence, mana, Willpower perhaps ? Are they tied to the occultist's &quot;status in the goetia's court&quot; (for lack of a better term for having a positive to neutral relationship with them) or are they permanent payments for services rendered ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-24-2022, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T14:58:30-07:00","id":1481866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia?p=1481851#post1481851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw an outline of that from the Dreaming Earth section of the <i>Astral Realms</i> book. Would there be anywhere else that the details are fleshed out or some sample Dreamborne are presented?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same book, p109-110, the sidebar on the &quot;Grant Influence&quot; Numen and the statblock of the Raccoon Master example Dreamborn it exists in. As the sidebar notes, it's common to all Animal Masters and Naturae, meaning it's conceivably fair game for any Influence based around an animal or environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would the Influences be fueled by Essence, mana, Willpower perhaps ? Are they tied to the occultist's &quot;status in the goetia's court&quot; (for lack of a better term for having a positive to neutral relationship with them) or are they permanent payments for services rendered ? </div> </div> </div>They are temporary boons in the same vein as the Aeons offering the Auctoritas Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T08:23:32-07:00","id":1481926,"title":"","content":"I think this might be a case where the canon as it stands is not strictly necessary. Across the range of the games, is there something like a form of Astral magic that a changeling might be allowed some form of access to (possibly limited) with the tutelage of a Goetia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T13:08:43-07:00","id":1481948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia?p=1481926#post1481926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this might be a case where the canon as it stands is not strictly necessary. Across the range of the games, is there something like a form of Astral magic that a changeling might be allowed some form of access to (possibly limited) with the tutelage of a Goetia?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not, for the reasons of &quot;the Astral is sufficiently niche that ritual sorcery involving it is limited to Mage and Beast, who get it from their own power and/or the primordial morphology of the Dreamtime&quot; and &quot;changelings do not interact with the Astral like other splats do and have powers whose design notes specify against having them work like ritual magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T14:43:15-07:00","id":1481952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481774-learning-from-goetia?p=1481926#post1481926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this might be a case where the canon as it stands is not strictly necessary. Across the range of the games, is there something like a form of Astral magic that a changeling might be allowed some form of access to (possibly limited) with the tutelage of a Goetia?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Satchel said, but\u2026.. maybe the section from Beast Player\u2019s Guide on manipulating the Bright Dream to affect the waking world\u2019s denizens\u2019 beliefs could be expanded upon and adapted to? It\u2019s a bit more hands-on than \u2018ritual\u2019 magic, so it <i>could</i> fit I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:36:42-07:00","id":1481977,"title":"","content":"You'd certainly struggle to find rituals like that - it would not be an easy task. But if any culture or tradition ever managed it, there'd be a Goetia in the Temenos representing them that might be able to impart some secrets. Alternatively, there are entities in the Anima Mundi that defy categorisation that may well know all sorts of things.<br /> <br /> And of course you could strike a deal with a Morphean for some forbidden knowledge.<br /> <br /> All of the above is absolutely stretching the limits of what a Changeling can do so make sure to discuss with your Storyteller. I'm not even sure how a Changeling would get into the Temenos, or the Anima Mundi - I'm sure there's gateways and holes somewhere, but these are going to be tricky to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/494367/The-Lost-Athanaeum?affiliate_id=1564482\" target=\"_blank\">The Lost Athanaeum</a> Mage adventure is now live on Storyteller's Vault!<br /> If you want to see it in play, check out <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500596-dimensions-unseen-mage-2e-actual-play-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">Dimensions Unseen</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27424-phoog","name":"Phoog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T02:10:33-07:00","id":1481985,"title":"","content":"There's a storytellers Vault product, 'A Deal with Darkness' which deals with making pacts with various beings, including Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}